 "source": "Good Sam directory (PUBLIC_PARK and local-named rows with no entry within 2 km), every named OSM tourism=camp_site/caravan_site with no entry within 1.5 km read by name, and the mycountyparks.com statewide Camping activity roster (173 parks) name-matched against the DB",
 "note": "50 adds on top of the 245 local entries IA already held - the largest single-state local yield so far. mycountyparks.com (the platform most Iowa county conservation boards book through) was the best instrument: its statewide Camping roster surfaced ~30 county campgrounds neither OSM nor Good Sam had. Also re-pinned Diamond Lake Park (id 3093), which sat a full degree north of Montezuma. Excluded: primitive/walk-in/equestrian county areas, the State Fair campground, Dutton's Cave/Goeken (1-2 electric sites). Held: Smidt Campground (Titonka - 82 full-hookup, city lists it but reviews name an owner) and Little Rock's Town & Country Park (no site count or hookups published). Private gap here is small next to the eastern states (Koch's Meadow Lake, Spook Cave, Pipe Dream, Miners Creek, Hildreth among ~20 unmatched).",
